From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 06:10:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: meson_gx_mmc: keep the 24 MHz cap for eMMC only

The 24 MHz cap from the previous patch is there for unreliable eMMC
reads on the ODROID-N2+, but it also holds the SD card at 24 MHz in
High Speed mode, about 11 MiB/s. Let the SD slot run at its DT
max-frequency instead (50 MHz on the ODROID-N2), about 21 MiB/s.

Tested on an ODROID-N2+: the eMMC stays at 24 MHz, the SD card
(SanDisk 256 GB) runs at 50 MHz; on 3 boots a 64 MiB raw read took
3.01 s and its crc32 matched the reference.

Signed-off-by: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
---
 drivers/mmc/meson_gx_mmc.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/meson_gx_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/meson_gx_mmc.c
index 082c77c9afe..211316c105c 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/meson_gx_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/meson_gx_mmc.c
@@ -357,6 +357,10 @@ static int meson_mmc_probe(struct udevice *dev)
 	 */
 	cfg->f_max = 24000000; /* 24 MHz */
 
+	/* The cap is for eMMC; let the SD slot run at its DT max-frequency. */
+	if (dev_read_bool(dev, "cap-sd-highspeed"))
+		cfg->f_max = dev_read_u32_default(dev, "max-frequency", 40000000);
+
 	cfg->b_max = 511; /* max 512 - 1 blocks */
 	cfg->name = dev->name;
 
